## Filters

Filters are made up of operators and operands.
Given an input note they return true or false.

Here are all the operators:

|-------------------------------------------------
| op1 & op2
| The *and* operator evals to true if both
|  the left and right operands eval to true.
|-------------------------------------------------
| op1 \| op2
| The *or* operator evals to true if either
|  the left or right operand evals to true.
|-------------------------------------------------
| ! op
| The *not* operator evals to true if it's
|  operand evals to false.
|-------------------------------------------------
| ()
| Use parens to change the evaluation order.
|-------------------------------------------------

Here are all the operands:

|-------------------------------------------------
| \*
| Evals to true for all notes.
|-------------------------------------------------
| \# \#1 \#2 ...
| A hash without a number evals to true if the
|  note has a priority. With a number it evals
|  to true if the note has the exact priority.
|-------------------------------------------------
| \@ \@foo
| A single @ evals to true if the note defines
|  at least 1 project tag. An @ with a word evals
|  to true if the note defines the exact tag.
|-------------------------------------------------
| 'some text'
| Text within single quotes evals to true
|  if the note contains the exact substring.
|-------------------------------------------------
| /some text/
| Text within forward slashes evals to true
|  if the note contains the substring fuzzily.
|-------------------------------------------------
| hide
| Evals to true if note has a *hide* attribute.
|  This filter only works if the entire filter
|  is of the form ``hide`` or ``hide & expr``.
|-------------------------------------------------
| x
| Evals to true if note is completed.
|-------------------------------------------------
| due
| Evals to true if note has a due date.
|-------------------------------------------------
| pin
| Evals to true if note is pinned.
|-------------------------------------------------

Here are some examples:

|-------------------------------------------------
| `@myproject & !#
| True for notes with an @myproject tag and no priority.
|-------------------------------------------------
| `due | #1
| True for notes with a due date or high priority.
|-------------------------------------------------
| 'hello' & x
| True for completed notes that contain 'hello'.
|-------------------------------------------------
